  "family": "cohomology",
  "summary": "Category of descent data is a particular presentation of a 2-categorical limit in Cat , i.e. the descent object , intended to solve the descent problem. It can be defined in severa",
  "detail": "Category of descent data is a particular presentation of a 2-categorical limit in Cat , i.e. the descent object , intended to solve the descent problem. It can be defined in several setups: in a formulation of descent via fibered categories and Grothendieck topologies , as well as in the (co) monadic descent . In the first case, the descent category appears as a presentation of the descent object , while in the (co)monadic descent the descent category is given by the Eilenberg-Moore category of the ( co ) monad . In a particular setup, the two approaches give the same result, see Bénabou-Roubaud theorem .\nnLab 页面共 2071 字符，含 8 个公式、39 个出链。",
