  "detail": "In SGA I.6 Grothendieck and Pierre Gabriel presented the formalism of fibered categories and descent; the exposition and the terminology emphasises a version of the relative point of view for categories. Thus they start with preliminaries over the slice 2-category Cat / C Cat/C of functors with fixed target category C C . Objects in Cat / C Cat/C are thus called categories over C C and the morphisms are called functors over C C . Standard passages between different slice categories are via the base change and the cobase change 2-functors.\nnLab 页面共 1897 字符，含 0 个公式、3 个出链。",
